# client portal logins (bcrypt hashes, never committed; see scripts/portal-user.mjs)
/portal-data/users.json

# iCloud sync conflict copies. This project lives in ~/Documents, which syncs,
# and a conflict leaves a "<name> 2.ts" beside the original. 35 of them were
# committed once, including stale copies of the auth and session code.
#
# The second pattern catches directories and extensionless files, which the first
# one misses because it requires a dot: "src/components/portal/admin 2" appeared
# on 26 Jul 2026 and was not ignored. iCloud also does this inside .git, where
# gitignore cannot help: a stray "refs/heads/<branch> 2" makes git fetch fail
# with "bad object", and git hides it as a broken ref name. Delete those by hand.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9]

# Tile pyramids ARE committed, because the portal serves the map from them and
# they have to reach Vercel. Do not add an ignore rule here: the layer route only
# serves a tile the manifest declares, so an ignored pyramid is a 404 on a
# deployed site with nothing wrong locally.
#
# Reproduce them with scripts/prepare-site.mjs, or export from QGIS/GDAL on the
# machine that holds the survey (context.md 8j and 8k). They stay small because
# empty tiles are never written: about 1 MB for Kotba, 17 MB for Aektanagar. Once
# a site passes the 50 MB trigger in 8h, that site moves to object storage and
# gets ignored here instead.

# Source terrain models the analysis API reads, symlinked to the gitignored
# survey folders above. Local only: in production these come from object storage
# via PORTAL_TERRAIN_DIR, and committing the symlinks would dangle on Vercel.
/portal-data/terrain/
